Year = {2019},
Pages = {4337-4344},
Note = {38th IAHR World Congress, Panama, PANAMA, SEP 01-06, 2019},
Organization = {Universidad Tecnologica de Panama; Universidad Latina de Panama},
Abstract = {Drought is one of the major natural disasters, it occurs frequently with
   wide range covering almost whole China. Drought affects agriculture,
   urban water supply and ecological environment, which has caused large
   losses in China. Drought monitoring and assessment is an important means
   of drought management for drought relief funds allocation, farmers' loss
   subsidy, drought relief emergency response initiation, media publicity
   and so on. This paper introduces the current situation, problems and
   prospects of drought monitoring and assessment in China. Then, the
   drought monitoring index, drought monitoring model and drought
   monitoring system are mainly presented. Moreover, the spatial-temporal
   continuity and accuracy of drought monitoring products are analyzed, and
   the effects of spatial resolution, land cover, irrigation and drought
   grading criteria on the accuracy of drought evaluation are discussed.
   Finally, the future application of drought monitoring and evaluation is
   prospected, and suggestions are put forward on the construction of
   comprehensive model, database and business platform for agricultural
   drought, urban drought and ecological drought.},
