   Turkey},
Abstract = {Cement production is one of the oldest industries in Turkey which has
   developed along with the urban growth. The surroundings of some of the
   oldest plants became urbanised so that people faced immediate contact
   with the air pollution problem.
   Air quality modelling techniques are in general very helpful in this
   respect provided the model is used properly with realible input data.
   EPA (Environmental Protection Agency) approved Breeze Air ISCLT3
   (Industrial Source Complex) software was applied to ten existing cement
   production plants. Air quality contribution of all the plants were fount
   to be below the Air Quality Protection Regulation (AQPR) limits.},
