Note = {Symposium on the Occasion of the VII International Congress of Ecology
   (INTECOL), FLORENCE, ITALY, JUL 19-25, 1998},
Organization = {Soc Human Ecol; Japanese \& Italian Soc Human Ecol},
Abstract = {The systemic relationship between human health and environmental factors
   in urban setting represents the focal point of concern for the modem
   public health in the postindustrial anthropological era, characterised
   by urbanisation.
   The `Healthy Cities Project' has been conceived and proposed by the WHO
   Regional Office for Europe in 1987 in order to implement principles and
   methodologies of human ecology in the management and promotion of urban
   health.
   Two main pillars are supporting the project on the spot:
   1. intersectoral action of the city's public and private agencies
   dealing with the factors of the `total environment' and with health
   determinants;
   2. community participation in supporting the control and promotion of
   environmental health and the promotion of healthy life-styles.
   The city of Padova, Italy, adopted the project and is still acting as a
   laboratory for trying new methods for identifying technical,
   professional, political obstacles; for resting information systems; for
   experimenting with new tools as such, for instance, healthy city
   profiles and plans.},
