Note = {9th International Conference on Modelling, Monitoring and Management of
   Air Pollution, ANCONA, ITALY, SEP 12-14, 2001},
Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; Ancona Univ},
Abstract = {The Environmental Psychology Research Unit together with the Fluids
   Research Centre, at the University of Surrey, UK, are investigating
   relationships between transport, air pollution and health. This
   collaborative research utilises a conceptual framework drawn from
   existing theories and paradigms in the field of environmental
   psychology, combined with analytical modelling and experimental data
   from fluid mechanics. The present research aims to investigate and
   account for actual and perceived levels of air pollution in Guildford,
   Surrey, with the collaboration of Guildford Borough Council.
   Preliminary research was carried out as a trial analysis to compare
   residents' spatial perceptions of air pollution in the Borough of
   Guildford with actual NO2 data. This was then plotted spatially using a
   GIS (Geographical Information System). On the basis of the results a
   research tool was developed which would allow for a more sophisticated
   analysis, and for advanced comparisons to be made between actual and
   perceived levels of air pollution. This paper presents the development
   of this methodology, involving a large-scale air pollution risk
   perception survey, which is to be carried out in the Guildford area.
   Respondents will be required to complete two tasks: a self-administered
   questionnaire and a cognitive mapping exercise. The questionnaire will
   be designed to gauge information on residents' knowledge, awareness and
   perceptions of risks in relation to air quality. The mapping exercise
   requires residents to plot on maps where they perceive air pollution to
   be in their local area. GIS will be used to plot the perceptual spatial
   representations of air pollution levels together with the actual
   real-time air quality data, in order to detect and identify disparities.},
