Organization = {Guangdong Univ Business Studies},
Abstract = {Heavy metal pollution is one of the main obstacles of municipal sewage
   treatment plant sludge for agricultural use. This paper gives an
   overview of four kinds of commonly used techniques for heavy metals
   removal in sewage sludge: chemical extraction, bioleaching,
   electrokinetic technology and solidification - stabilization, also
   analyzed the future direction of development.
   With the development of our country, the problems of environment are
   gradually standing out. The number of urban sewage treatment plants
   increase quickly, resulting in sludge yield increase, how to reasonable
   disposal of sludge, prevent the second time pollution has drawn
   attention of the world. Municipal sludge refers to the urban sewage,
   industrial waste water treatment of solid waste, is the municipal sewage
   treatment plant for recurrent product. Municipal sludge contains a lot
   of organic matter and rich in nitrogen, phosphorus and other nutrients.
   Some studies have shown Ell sludge can increase soil fertility; improve
   soil organic matter and nitrogen, phosphorus content. Agriculture sludge
   is considered the most development potential disposal with China's
   national conditions. However, the sludge is rich in nutrients, while
   also adsorption concentrated heavy metals, according to the report
   {[}2], the majority of our city content of heavy metals in sludge up to
   hundreds to thousands of mg / kg, and its agricultural easy on soil
   groundwater, flora and fauna cause secondary pollution and potential
   ecological risk. Therefore, heavy metal contamination of municipal
   sludge is one of the main obstacles to restricting the sludge for
   agricultural. To make municipal sludge resources and being harmless, It
   Is Essential to remove heavy metals in the sludge fundamentally.},
