   Minist Educ},
Abstract = {Near-infrared spectroscopy (NIRS) is a new technique applied in
   neuroscience. This study used NIRS technique to examine prefrontal
   responses to emotional words, non-emotional words and non-words. We
   found that the difference between the oxy-HB response elicited by
   negative words and the other conditions was significant (p < .05).
   Within the other conditions, the oxy-HB value did not show a significant
   difference (p > .1). The emotional words elicited greater oxy-HB
   response than the non-emotional words or stimuli.},
