   Univ Agr Akad, Noreikiskes, LITHUANIA, OCT 15-17, 2009},
Abstract = {Aim of research - to assess the farm diversification role in rural
   development. The research revealed that farm diversification has direct
   and indirect, positive and negative effects on the rural economy,
   environmental protection, and relations among people. The research
   showed that new jobs are usually created for family members or urban
   citizens. Country people are usually engaged in low-qualified jobs. The
   impact of diversification of the sociocultural and natural environment
   of rural areas typically depends on the moral values of people, which
   predetermine the life quality of the person and the community as a
   whole.},
