   (ICEEP 2013), Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, APR 19-21, 2013},
Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ; Chinese Acad Sci, Res Ctr Eco Environm Sci, Key Lab
   Environm Biotechnol},
Abstract = {With the acceleration of urbanization, dust composed of solid particles
   has become one of the major air pollutants in urban areas. The
   dust-retention capacity and its spatial distribution of 8 greenbelt
   types are discussed. The results show that the dust-retention capacity
   of Cedrus deodara is the highest, and the total dust-retention capacity
   is (2.85 +/- 0.28) g/m(2), in contrast, only (0.48 +/- 0.04) g/m(2) for
   Ligustrum quihold. Moreover, the dust-retention capacity of outside of 7
   greenbelt types is higher than that of inside, except Osmanthus
   fragrans. The dust-retention capability of outside indicates an order of
   lower section, middle section and upper section, and an order of middle
   section, lower section and upper section of inside.},
