   Ryerson Univ, Toronto, CANADA, JUL 19-21, 2019},
Organization = {Ted Rogers Sch Management; SocialMediaLab.ca},
Abstract = {The position of this paper is that sentiment analysis lacks construct
   validity: it systematically fails to measure emotions in text. This
   position is elaborated through theoretical examination of the existing
   approach, which is shown to allow only rough correlates of emotion
   confounded with other properties of texts. Crude correlates are regarded
   by this critique as unacceptable in the absence of a theory capable of
   guiding their improvement. An alternative statistical approach for
   analysis of sentiment in text is proposed, along with discussion of how
   it would need to be developed.},
