Series = {Energy and Environmental Engineering Series},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {311+},
Note = {5th International Conference on Energy, Environment, Ecosystems and
   Sustainable Development/2nd International Conference on Landscape
   Architecture, Vouliagmeni, GREECE, SEP 28-30, 2009},
Abstract = {In Iranian mind, garden has a pervasive picture as it has changed into
   an internal view through centuries and is considered part of its
   culture. From one side Iranian Gardens got their feature and shape from
   their geometric and structural definitions and from harmony of their
   sustainable orders. As each of these orders were modern but an unwritten
   principle and norm that systematized definition, planning, shaping and
   forming of a part of garden in relation with other parts of it. This
   order was in such an extent that no Iranian Garden is designed except if
   it included both orders of structure and geometrical point and forming
   Iranian architecture space, elements and arena. Investigating
   experiences of Iranian urban design in relation with methods of
   exploiting garden in urban structure and spaces can have significant
   role in reconstruction, repair and development of cities. Therefore, we
   have tried in this article to analyze basics of landscape architecture
   and Iranian Garden Urbanism together with its teachings in contemporary
   garden design of Iran from different points of view.},
