   17-21, 2003},
Organization = {IEEE Engn Med \& Biol Soc; Coral; Univ Autonome Metropolitana; Sandia
   Natl Lab},
Abstract = {The aim of the current study is the conception of a tool to analyze the
   pupillary dynamics. The reading of the pupil motion is a well-know
   method that provides functional information about the autonomous nervous
   system. The monitoring is made up of three parts. First, a digital
   camera is chosen for the image acquisition because of its simple use at
   the patient's bed and its low cost. Then a software estimates the
   pupillogram, i.e. the plot of the pupil area versus time, from the
   digital video sequence using deformable templates. And finally, the
   pupil light reflex (PLR) is modeled by a second order linear system to
   compute characteristic parameters. They can be used to diagnose various
   affections from a statistical analysis.},
