   Association-for-Advancement-of-Behavior-Therapy, TORONTO, CANADA, NOV
   11-14, 1999},
Organization = {Assoc Advancement Behav Therapy},
Abstract = {Experiential avoidance is the unwillingness to experience unwanted
   thoughts, emotions, or bodily sensations and an individual's attempts to
   alter, avoid, or escape those experiences. The aim of the current
   studies was to broaden previous research indicating that experiential
   avoidance often leads to the development and maintenance of
   psychological distress. Results indicated that experiential avoidance is
   significantly correlated with psychological distress and post-traumatic
   symptomatology over and above other measures of psychological
   functioning. Limitations and implications for treatment and prevention
   of psychological distress are discussed. (C) 2004 Elsevier Ltd. All
   rights reserved.},
