   TUT Wuri Handayani; RISTEK BRIN},
Abstract = {Ecotourism is environmentally friendly tourism with the activities of
   watching, studying, admiring nature, flora and fauna, socio-cultural
   local ethnicity, and fostering the preservation of the natural
   environment by involving local residents. Rokan Hulu is a regency in
   Riau Province, Indonesia. Ecotourism is not a major sector in this area,
   however, this regency has some natural locations that might be
   developed. This study aimed to identify and analysed natural ecotourism
   objects in this area. The locations and respondents was nominated by
   using purposive sampling method. Respondents consisted of local people,
   tourists, tourism businesses, and stakeholders. The collected data was
   associated with the concept of 4A (attraction, amenity, accessibility,
   and ancillary service) and SWOT (strength, weakness, opportunity and
   threat) analysed, WTA (willing to accept) and WTP ( willing to pay), and
   descriptive potential analysis natural ecotourism economy. Some
   ecotourism objects in this area were identified, namely Aek Martua
   Waterfall Ecourism, Batu Gajah Ecourism, Huta Sikapir Cave Ecotourism,
   and Hapanasan Natural Hot Springs. It is recommended to improve
   facilities and infrastructure access to each location and the main
   object of natural ecotourism is managed by professionals by involving
   local communities.},
