Note = {13th International Multidisciplinary Scientific Geoconference, SGEM
   2013, Albena, BULGARIA, JUN 16-22, 2013},
Abstract = {The article discusses the air quality in rural areas. The paper aims to
   quantify the sources of air pollution by solid particles, and to carry
   out emission and imission assessment of air quality in standardized
   rural areas. The model village consisted of 35 residential buildings and
   road, without industrial activities. The actual state can be verified
   only by measurement of imissions, which is costly. The means of
   evaluation are mathematical models of air quality. It was expected that
   air quality in rural areas in the winter heating season is comparable to
   normal values in the urban environment. Model calculations showed that
   the winter heating period has a significant impact on the rural air
   quality in terms of PM10. The calculated mean values were almost 60\% of
   value measured in the city of Kosice, (Sturova station). The findings
   make it desirable to use ecologically sound energy resources.},
