Note = {3rd European Conference on Flood Risk Management (FLOODrisk), Lyon,
   FRANCE, OCT 17-21, 2016},
Abstract = {For several years now, building resilient and building sustainable are
   two of the main challenges of urban planning in cities. Though, both
   challenges are usually treated separately at the operational scale,
   which may imply antagonisms or synergies. From a review of the
   literature, this paper highlights the fact that there is a need to
   ``decompartmentalise{''} researches on resilience and energy efficiency
   to provide integrated professional tools for the design of future urban
   developments, especially in flood zones. In order to improve both
   resilience and energy efficiency, it appears that networks are key
   elements.},
