Abstract = {Many countries agree to sustainable development principles. In China,
   urbanization is regarded as an important strategy for urban growth. As a
   result, the number of city has increased rapidly in recent years,
   especially medium-sized cities, which have prominent status in the
   Chinese urban system. Along with the fast urbanization, traffic
   problemes become serious more and more. Medium-sized cities have
   differetn characteristics in terms of technology, capital, and
   population, thus, different methods should be used to deal with traffic
   problemes in such cities in comparison with big cities and small towns.
   In this paper, the authors firstly discuss the current status, problems
   and the causes of traffic problems in Chinese medium-sized cities, and
   provide several suggestions to achieve green transportation, i.e.
   increasing bus expansion ability, encouraging flexible way to travel,
   establishing sustainable ``green{''} structure of a city; emphasizing
   policy prevention, and promoting green traffic in the context of
   low-carbon economy.},
