Abstract = {CHRONIC violence is a growing problem in our society today as evidenced,
   among other factors, by the ever-increasing murder rate in many of our
   large urban centers in the United States. Emphasis has begun to be
   placed on chronic violence, causes that may contribute to it, and the
   impact of this violence on cities and the country at large. While
   concern has been expressed, we still have not addressed adequately, nor
   do we fully understand, the effects on the children who must grow up in
   environments where they are repeatedly being exposed to significant
