   Using Fuzzy Comprehensive Assessment},
Booktitle = {DYNAMICS OF URBAN AGGLOMERATION IN CHINA: PREFERENCES OF ENERGY-SAVING
   AND ENVIRONMENT-FRIENDLY SOCIETY},
Year = {2009},
Pages = {125-129},
Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Based on the principle of fuzzy mathematics, the fuzzy comprehensive
   assessing model for evaluating surface water quality was established.
   The model could not only embody systemic and synthetic characters but
   also simplify the calculation. Selecting 13 assessment factors, the
   fuzzy comprehensive assessment method was applied to assess water
   quality at 10 different monitoring sections of Gan River in NanChang
   section, which supplied scientific evidence for environment management
   and environment decision. According to the assessment results, water
   qualities of 8 monitoring sections reached I level and 2 monitoring
   sections reached V level. Generally, the water quality of Gan River in
   NanChang section is satisfactory but there is a deteriorating trend.
   Compared with traditional comprehensive pollution index assessment, the
   water quality level classified according to the fuzzy comprehensive
   assessment much more conforms to objective reality of the water quality.},
